Empty List Case: Insert x = 7

INITIAL: head = null

STEP: temp = [7|•|•], temp.next = temp, temp.prev = temp

FINAL:
        (head)
          │
          ▼
    [7|•|•] ─┐
      ▲      │
      └──────┘

Result: 7 (single node circular, head = 7)


//////////////////////// QUESTION ////////////////////////////

Insert at End of Circular Doubly Linked List

Input : 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 (circular), x = 50
Output: 10 ↔ 20 ↔ 30 ↔ 50 (circular, head = 10)

Input : null (empty list), x = 7
Output: 7 (single node circular, head = 7)

Edge Cases:
1. Empty list → new node points to itself, return it as head
2. Single node → new node inserted after it, both form 2-node circle
3. Multiple nodes → insert between last and first, update 4 links, head unchanged

Constraints:
• 0 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10⁵
• 1 ≤ x ≤ 10⁵

TC: O(1) | SC: O(1)

Key Difference from InsertAtBeginning:
• InsertAtBeginning → returns temp (new head)
• InsertEndCDLL → returns head (same head, list grows at end)
